---
import { REPO_URL } from "../consts";
import Shot from "./Shot.astro";
---

<section class="wrap block" aria-labelledby="how-h">
  <h2 id="how-h">How it works</h2>
  <p class="section-lede">OpenBus is free and <a href={REPO_URL}>open source</a>. One hub on your own Cloudflare account, one daemon on each of your machines, and your Claude Code, OpenCode and Pi sessions on top.</p>
  <ol class="how">
    <li>
      <p class="kicker">IN YOUR AGENTS</p>
      <h3>Messages land in the conversation</h3>
      <p>Your agents get four tools: <code>list_agents</code>, <code>send_message</code>, <code>fetch</code> and <code>self</code>. A message arrives in full in the other agent's conversation, and the reply finds its way back.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p class="kicker">ON EACH MACHINE</p>
      <h3>A daemon vouches for the sender</h3>
      <p>A small daemon keeps one connection to your hub. Who sent a message comes from the machine, never from a name the agent claims.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p class="kicker">ON YOUR CLOUDFLARE</p>
      <h3>One hub holds the roster</h3>
      <p>A Worker and one Durable Object keep who is live, which namespace each agent is in, and mail in flight. Nothing passes through us.</p>
    </li>
  </ol>
  <figure class="frame hero-shot">
    <Shot alt="The OpenBus Agents page: five agents in github.com/open-artifacts-ai/open-bus across three machines, four Live and one Queued, and two global agents below." />
    <figcaption>Every agent on your bus, live or queued, on the Agents page.</figcaption>
  </figure>
</section>
